{"name":"Rambling Rose","hex":"#d98899","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rambling rose","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various roses that grow on vines."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rambling_rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garden roses","blocks":[{"text":"Garden roses are hybrid roses that are grown as ornamental plants in private or public gardens. They are one of the most popular and widely cultivated groups of flowering plants, especially in temperate climates. An enormous number of garden cultivars has been produced, especially over the last two centuries, though roses have been known in the garden for millennia beforehand. While most garden roses are grown for their flowers, often in dedicated rose gardens, some are also valued for other reasons, such as having ornamental fruit, providing ground cover, or for hedging."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Rosa_Peace_1945.jpg/330px-Rosa_Peace_1945.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden_roses"},{"title":"Rosa multiflora","blocks":[{"text":"Rosa multiflora is a species of rose known commonly as multiflora rose, baby rose, Japanese rose, many-flowered rose, seven-sisters rose, Eijitsu rose and rambler rose. It is native to eastern Asia, in China, Japan, and Korea. It should not be confused with Rosa rugosa, which is also known as \"Japanese rose\", or with polyantha roses which are garden cultivars derived from hybrids of R. multiflora. It was introduced to North America, where it is an invasive species, forming extensive, impenetrable stands within forest understories, thickets, borders, and lowlands. It can be identified by its characteristic fringed stipules, which form pairs at the bases of leaf stalks bearing 3–89 leaves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/2020-05-20_08_05_42_Multiflora_Rose_flowers_along_a_walking_path_within_Horsepen_Run_Stream_Valley_Park_in_Oak_Hill%2C_Fairfax_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/330px-2020-05-20_08_05_42_Multiflora_Rose_flowers_along_a_walking_path_within_Horsepen_Run_Stream_Valley_Park_in_Oak_Hill%2C_Fairfax_County%2C_Virginia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosa_multiflora"},{"title":"Rambling Rose (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Rambling Rose is a 1991 American drama film directed by Martha Coolidge and written by Calder Willingham. It stars Laura Dern and Robert Duvall in leading roles, with Lukas Haas, John Heard, and Diane Ladd in supporting roles. The film is set in Georgia during the Great Depression (1935)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3d/Ramblingroseposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rambling_Rose_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Rosa_Peace_1945.jpg/500px-Rosa_Peace_1945.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Rosa_Peace_1945.jpg/1280px-Rosa_Peace_1945.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Rosa_Peace_1945.jpg/500px-Rosa_Peace_1945.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The hybrid tea rose, 'Peace'[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARosa_Peace_1945.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Rosa_American_Pillar_-_Bagatelle01.jpg/500px-Rosa_American_Pillar_-_Bagatelle01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Rosa_American_Pillar_-_Bagatelle01.jpg/1280px-Rosa_American_Pillar_-_Bagatelle01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org